  "caption": "Nephew Ollie, 10, plays tennis. Only tennis. Every day, all year. Then the niggles started and the fun faded.\n\nPlaying one sport all year in childhood is linked to more overuse injuries and burnout, and it doesn't reliably make better athletes. Early specialisation isn't needed to reach the top.\n\nWhat can help: playing more than one sport until the mid-teens, several weeks off each sport a year plus 1–2 rest days a week, counting total load across every team and coach, a rough guide of weekly organised hours no more than the child's age, and supervised strength training.\n\nGet it checked for pain beyond a couple of weeks, limping, night pain, lost enjoyment, sleep or mood changes, or frequent minor injuries.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
